       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n**The problem:** Amlodipine 50 mg is 5 times the usual maximum adult dose. Normal dosing is:\n- Starting dose: 5 mg by mouth once daily (2.5 mg for frail or elderly patients, or those with liver impairment)\n- Maximum: 10 mg once daily\n\nA 50 mg dose would put this patient at risk of severe low blood pressure, a reflex fast heart rate and shock. Amlodipine overdoses are hard to treat because the drug stays in the body so long. This is very likely a typo for **5 mg**, since a misplaced zero is a common error.\n\n**Please confirm which you meant:**\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily.** I can enter this right away.\n2. **A different dose** (e.g., 2.5 mg or 10 mg).\n3. **50 mg is correct and intentional.** If so, please give the clinical reason. I'd also recommend having a pharmacist check it before the order is entered."
