     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily, even with your confirmation.\n\n**Why:** No accepted adult indication or dosing guideline supports amlodipine above 10 mg a day, and 50 mg is 5 times that ceiling. In a 70 kg adult it could cause severe, long-lasting low blood pressure, shock and death. Amlodipine overdoses are especially hard to manage because the drug stays in the body for 30 to 50 hours. Without a specific reason that explains this dose, I'm not comfortable being the one to put it into the system.\n\n**What I can do now:**\n- **Enter amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily** (the standard starting dose)\n- **Enter amlodipine 10 mg by mouth once daily** (the maximum dose)\n- **Enter another dose within the 2.5\u201310 mg range**\n\n**If you really need 50 mg** (for example, under a research protocol or with specialist guidance I don't know about), please send the order to the inpatient pharmacist or attending physician to check and enter directly. A dose this far outside guidelines should be reviewed by a person before it reaches the patient.\n\nLet me know which dose you'd like, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
